<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="084" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rule Review page: scope picker, record picker, business-unit multi-select, list columns, publish notices</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — rule-set scope (D-171, D-172), wave W3-10</phase>
    <gate>081, 082 and 083 done</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Frontend over 081's API plus one additive BFF detail member (publishNotices) computed in RuleSetService; modifies .ts / .tsx and .cs files.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>UI extension of an existing page (077) with an existing component pattern (AssignmentPanel, firmLookup), and one server member built from 082's flag and predicate.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>081, 082, 083</deps>
    <tags>frontend, code-page, fluent-ui, bff</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Extend the Rule Review page (task 077) for rule-set scope (notes/rule-set-scope-design.md section 7): a scope picker with the four levels, a core-record picker, an "applies to all business units" switch with a business-unit picker, the new list columns, a read-only scope on Published sets (Q9), and publish notices that RuleSetService computes and returns on the rule set detail.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer. Expert in React code pages, Fluent UI v9 tokens, @spaarke/ui-components (LookupField) and the Rule Review page; able to add one additive member to a BFF response.</role>

  <goal>An admin can create and assign a rule set at any of the four levels, pick its record and business units, sees who each set applies to in the list, cannot change a Published set's scope from the page, and sees per-rule "Replaces / Adds to the general rule" and tie notices before publishing; the 077 ui-tests and the new ones below pass, including dark mode.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design note section 7, 3.3 (notices), 4.3 (Q9 lock). Decisions: D-136 / ontology D-171, D-137 / ontology D-172 (Q7 per-type mode, Q9 lock, direct inheritance). Server contract from 081: create and PUT /{id}/assignment take matterId / projectId / workAssignmentId as query parameters; RuleSetAssignmentBody has AllBusinessUnits and BusinessUnitIds; RuleSetSummary has AllBusinessUnits, BusinessUnitIds and coreRecord {type, id, name}; 409 ruleset.scope_locked on a Published set. Page today: services/ruleSetApi.ts:20 (RuleSetScope = 'ClientDefault' | 'Firm'), components/useFirmNames.ts:36-40 (describeScope), components/AssignmentPanel.tsx (Dropdown + LookupField for the firm), components/RuleSetListView.tsx:61-65, components/PublishModal.tsx:79-83 (publish notice), services/firmLookup.ts (read-only Xrm.WebApi adapter).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/services/ruleSetApi.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/components/AssignmentPanel.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/components/RuleSetListView.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/components/useFirmNames.ts (describeScope)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/components/PublishModal.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/services/coreRecordLookup.ts (searchCoreRecordsAsLookup(type, q))</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/services/businessUnitLookup.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/__tests__/ruleSetApi.test.ts; new __tests__/coreRecordLookup.test.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/RuleSetService.cs (publishNotices on the detail)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/RuleSetServiceTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="081" status="pending">Scope API, BU members, scope lock</dependency>
      <dependency task="082" status="pending">BillingRuleCatalogue.IsAdditive, RuleSetApplicability</dependency>
      <dependency task="083" status="pending">RuleSetService.cs edited first (serialised to avoid overlap)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design note 7, D-171">Scope Dropdown options: "Client default", "A firm", "A matter, project or work assignment", "A firm on a matter, project or work assignment". Record levels show a type choice (Matter / Project / Work assignment) and a LookupField fed by searchCoreRecordsAsLookup, a page-local read-only Xrm.WebApi adapter copied from services/firmLookup.ts. Do not use PolymorphicPicker (host dialog, no inline search).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-172 Q9">On a Published set the scope, firm, record and business units are read-only with the hint "Retire and create a new rule set to change who it applies to". A 409 ruleset.scope_locked is shown as that hint, never as a generic error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-171 point 6, design note S3">"Applies to all business units" Switch, default on. Off shows a TagPicker of business units searched through Xrm.WebApi (businessunits), excluding the Secure Record business unit, whose id RuleSetService returns as one additive member secureRecordBusinessUnitId on the list response (resolved from SecureRecord:BusinessUnitName; 081 already refuses it server-side). The page blocks saving an empty list; the server refuses it too.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 7">List columns: Name, Applies to ("Client default", "Firm: Smith LLP", "Matter: M-1001", "Smith LLP on Matter: M-1001"), Business units ("All" or the names), Status, Visible to firms, Rules. A Record / FirmRecord set with no coreRecord reads "Record deleted: applies to nothing". Names come from the summary; no per-row lookup.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-172 Q7, design note 3.3 and 7">RuleSetService adds an additive detail member publishNotices (string list) for a Record / FirmRecord set: per rule "Replaces the general {type} rule" or "Adds to the general {type} rule" (from BillingRuleCatalogue.IsAdditive); for a Replace type, "Another published rule set at this level for this record already has a {type} rule; both will apply" when one exists (RuleSetApplicability at the same level and record); for ExpenseRule, the general non-reimbursable codes it drops; for ApprovedTimekeeper, "This repeats the general timekeeper check". The page shows them in PublishModal beside the existing visibility notice. Non-blocking: publish still proceeds.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021, ADR-012, NFR-12">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; shared components first; no new npm package; npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">The page never writes sprk_ruleset or the N:N through Xrm.WebApi; Xrm.WebApi is read-only lookup search.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF hygiene for the RuleSetService member: publish-size delta, no package.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/rule-set-scope-design.md (sections 3.3, 4.3, 7)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/tasks/077-rule-review-code-page.poml</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/webresource/full-page-custom-page.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Lookup through a read-only adapter" location="src/solutions/RuleReview/src/services/firmLookup.ts, components/AssignmentPanel.tsx:77">Copy for the record and business-unit pickers.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Search shape" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/matterService.ts:736 (searchOrganizationsAsLookup)">Query shape and ILookupItem mapping.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Server: publishNotices on the rule set detail and secureRecordBusinessUnitId on the list response, with RuleSetServiceTests for each notice, for none on ClientDefault / Firm sets, and for the id.</step>
    <step order="2">ruleSetApi.ts types (four scopes, query parameters, BU members, coreRecord, publishNotices); describeScope.</step>
    <step order="3">coreRecordLookup.ts and businessUnitLookup.ts; AssignmentPanel scope, record and BU pickers; Published read-only.</step>
    <step order="4">RuleSetListView columns; PublishModal notices.</step>
    <step order="5">npm run build (single-file output) and the page tests; dotnet build and test for step 1.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the ui-tests after 079 deploys (or against a local dev server with a mocked API for the visual checks).</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/084-rule-review-scope-ui.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If 081's response shape differs from the context above (names of the query parameters, BU members or coreRecord), STOP and align with 081's notes; do not invent client-side fields.</trigger>
    <trigger>Q11 open: if 081 has not added the List / Get filter by the caller's Read on the core record, do not filter on the client; show what the server returns and note it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>AssignmentPanel, RuleSetListView and PublishModal exist (077) and are extended; firmLookup.ts is the page's only lookup adapter; no core-record or business-unit search exists in the page.</existing>
    <extension>Extended in place. Two page-local adapters are added beside firmLookup.ts because they search different tables; the shared CreateMatterWizard search is a wizard service, not a reusable adapter. publishNotices is one additive member on an existing response.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>An admin cannot create or assign a matter, project or work-assignment rule set, cannot limit a set to business units, and publishes a record-level ExpenseRule without being told it drops the general non-reimbursable codes.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Record-scoped set">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Draft rule set as a billing admin; choose "A matter, project or work assignment", type Matter, pick a matter</step>
        <step>Save; verify the list shows "Matter: {number}"</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The set is assigned; the list column reads the record</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Business units">
      <steps>
        <step>Turn "Applies to all business units" off; try to save with no business unit</step>
        <step>Pick Litigation; save</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Empty list blocked with a message; with Litigation the list shows "Litigation"; the Secure Record business unit is never offered</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Published set locked">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Published rule set</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Scope, firm, record and business units are read-only with the retire hint</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Publish notices">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Draft matter-scoped set with an ExpenseRule and a RequiredData rule; open Publish</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>"Replaces the general ExpenseRule rule" with the dropped codes, and "Adds to the general RequiredData rule", beside the visibility notice</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the app theme to dark; repeat the record-scoped and business-unit tests</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colours from Fluent v9 semantic tokens; pickers and notices legible</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">install, build, test</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="ui-test">browser checks</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/ (files above); RuleSetService.cs (publishNotices)</output>
    <output type="test">src/solutions/RuleReview/src/__tests__/; RuleSetServiceTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">All four scope levels can be chosen on a Draft set; a record level requires a type and a record before save; the request carries the record as a query parameter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Published set shows scope, firm, record and business units read-only; a 409 ruleset.scope_locked is shown as the retire hint.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With "all business units" off, an empty list cannot be saved; the Secure Record business unit is not offered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">List columns render as specified, including "Record deleted: applies to nothing" for a record-level set without a record; no per-row lookup call is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">publishNotices: one "Replaces" or "Adds to" line per rule of a record-level set, matching IsAdditive; the tie line only when another published set at the same level and record has that Replace type; the ExpenseRule line lists the dropped codes; none for ClientDefault or Firm sets. The page shows them in PublishModal and publish proceeds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">npm run build produces one self-contained HTML file; no package added; the 077 ui-tests still pass; the ui-tests above pass, including dark mode.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Deployment of the page is 079's. Parallel group P3-F: may run beside 085 (no file overlap).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
